{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":477658,"name":"Russ","username":"Russ","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/russ/{size}/119174_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-29T14:44:57.970Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e“It’s a known Grok Bot bug, not Tailscale and not missing Administrator. Chat can stay up while the local-computer hook never registers. Staff’s own note: the helper starts, then drops its connection to their servers. There’s no attach button you can press.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOf course this failed after I registered for a 1 yr sub - coincidentally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlways reproduceable.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocal computer access., which is set to “Always allow”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows 10/11\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.30\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt-in\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-477658-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-477658-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-08-30T11:04:55.673Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":137,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":687.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Russ","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135140,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":477704,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-29T15:53:48.317Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the report. What you’re describing matches an issue we’re tracking. The helper that connects Grok Bot to your local computer starts, but doesn’t finish registration, so chat keeps working but local computer access stays unavailable. I’ve shared your case with the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA reset like this usually helps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot. Right-click the tray icon and click Quit, not just closing the window.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Task Manager and end any remaining Grok Bot processes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLaunch Grok Bot again and give it a couple minutes to reconnect.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf your local computer still doesn’t show up, sign out and sign back in in Grok Bot. That fully recreates the helper. Version 0.31.0 is also rolling out now, so it’s worth checking for an update and upgrading.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis isn’t related to your subscription. On our side it’s active and looks fine. This is specifically about the helper reconnecting after an update.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know how it goes. If it still doesn’t help, we’ll dig deeper.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-08-29T15:53:48.317Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":11,"readers_count":10,"score":27.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":478367,"name":"Russ","username":"Russ","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/russ/{size}/119174_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-30T17:09:02.666Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eFixed, thank-you Dean\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-08-30T17:09:02.666Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":4,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":21.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Russ","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135140,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":500001,"name":"Cem Güzel","username":"Cem_Guzel","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/8491ac/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-24T12:25:06.890Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSame class of issue on Windows. Phone Grok Bot works on the same account; desktop does not.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows Grok Bot 0.58.0\u003cbr\u003e\nSplash: “Grok Bot is having trouble connecting” / retry greyed out\u003cbr\u003e\nIn-app Check for Updates fails: “Could not check for updates”\u003cbr\u003e\nIn-app Send Feedback also fails\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNetwork from this PC is fine:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ecurl --noproxy “*” -I \u003ca href=\"https://api2.cursor.sh\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://api2.cursor.sh\u003c/a\u003e → HTTP 200\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003enslookup test123.us8/us10.cursorvm.com OK (1.1.1.1)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ecurl those hosts → 404 awselb/2.0\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Reset from the UI failed with the partial-state dialog. I did not retry Reset.\u003cbr\u003e\nSupport ticket T-G14434. Sam said the cloud computer is healthy (phone works), this is a Windows client/session problem after the failed partial Reset, and passed it to a human.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease don’t Reset the Agent Computer. Happy to add screenshots.\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/9/7/975b2a983000fa6bfc00deff3dc0800da83b5635.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/lAXq6LMtdpc0WYKI7SDHvAUsJtr.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/7/975b2a983000fa6bfc00deff3dc0800da83b5635_2_690x494.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"lAXq6LMtdpc0WYKI7SDHvAUsJtr\" width=\"690\" height=\"494\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/7/975b2a983000fa6bfc00deff3dc0800da83b5635_2_690x494.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/7/975b2a983000fa6bfc00deff3dc0800da83b5635_2_1035x741.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/7/975b2a983000fa6bfc00deff3dc0800da83b5635_2_1380x988.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F8F8F8\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1602×1149 39 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T12:25:06.890Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Cem Güzel","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://api2.cursor.sh","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":139601,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":500031,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-24T13:45:50.745Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed diagnostic report. That really helps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour case is different from the original topic in this thread. Your cloud computer looks healthy since the phone on the same account works. What’s failing is the Windows desktop client after an unsuccessful partial Reset. This looks like a client or session issue on the desktop side, not a network problem. Your curl and nslookup results look clean, and a 404 from awselb on the cursorvm hosts is a normal load balancer response.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince you already opened T-G14434 and a teammate joined, that’s the right channel. Please keep going there, and it’s also a good place to attach screenshots.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor now, don’t touch Reset or Recover, since it already put things into a partial state. Here’s a safe, non-destructive way to reset the desktop session.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully close Grok Bot. Right-click the tray icon and choose Quit, not just closing the window.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Task Manager, end any remaining Grok Bot processes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLaunch it again and give it a couple minutes to reconnect.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf that doesn’t help, sign out and sign in inside the app. This recreates the local session and unlike Reset it doesn’t touch the cloud computer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know how it goes.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T13:45:50.745Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":139601,"username":"Cem_Guzel","name":"Cem Güzel","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/8491ac/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/9","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":500095,"name":"Russ","username":"Russ","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/russ/{size}/119174_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-24T15:23:00.000Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThe problem was fixed later that day. The issue can be considered closed.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":6,"updated_at":"2026-09-24T15:23:19.165Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":9,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":169924,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","display_username":"Russ","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":135140,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"via_email":true,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer/169924/10","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[477658,477704,478367,500001,500031,500095]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,26],[3,25],[4,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":407,"name":"remote-control","slug":"remote-control"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot cannot access my local computer","id":169924,"title":"Grok Bot cannot access my local computer","posts_count":6,"created_at":"2026-08-29T14:44:57.894Z","views":210,"reply_count":2,"like_count":1,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-24T15:23:00.000Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-cannot-access-my-local-computer","category_id":6,"word_count":680,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":135140,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_169924","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":10,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked":false,"topic_timer":null,"message_bus_last_id":10,"participant_count":3,"show_read_indicator":false,"thumbnails":null,"slow_mode_enabled_until":null,"tags_disable_ads":false,"related_topics":[{"fancy_title"